{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.068,
   "text": "I guard a small art museum at night. Forty paintings, one long hallway... and me."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.668,
   "end": 14.212,
   "text": "The old guard left me one rule, scratched into the back of my badge."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.812,
   "end": 21.127,
   "text": "The woman in the gray portrait always looks at the window. If she ever looks at you... don't look away first."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.027,
   "end": 28.277,
   "text": "For two months, she just stared at that window. Pale face. Gray dress. Hands folded in her lap."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.977,
   "end": 33.564,
   "text": "Then, one rainy night, I swept my flashlight across her frame..."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 34.464,
   "end": 36.896,
   "text": "And her eyes were on me."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.496,
   "end": 43.872,
   "text": "I froze. I stared back. My eyes burned, and watered... and I didn't dare blink."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.672,
   "end": 48.021,
   "text": "Then my radio crackled, right on my belt."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.021,
   "end": 52.837,
   "text": "I looked down. Just for a second."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.737,
   "end": 56.852,
   "text": "When I looked up... the frame was empty."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.052,
   "end": 64.236,
   "text": "Then everything went cold. And still. And I couldn't lift my hands from my lap."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.836,
   "end": 71.767,
   "text": "They hired a new guard this week. Young. Nervous. He reads the back of his badge every night."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.567,
   "end": 78.263,
   "text": "Tonight, he walked past with his flashlight... and I turned my eyes from the window... to him."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 79.663,
   "end": 82.201,
   "text": "Please... don't look away first."
  }
 ],
